  "notes": "Transcribed from the official Lincoln University 2026-2027 Academic Year Catalog. DBA: 54 units required core (18 courses x 3 units) + 24 units concentration + 3 units doctoral research seminar (BA 501) + 12 units dissertation (BA 597/598/599) = 93 units. Concentration shown is International Business (first-listed of three: IB, Finance and Investments, Human Resources Management): choose five 4-unit 400-level courses (BA 413, BA 414, BA 415, BA 416, BA 417 — the first five listed) plus the required BA 481 Graduate Internship and Report in IB. The catalog publishes no quarter-by-quarter sequence for the DBA (only a year-by-year narrative); the layout below is a prerequisite-respecting 13-semester arrangement. Catalog inconsistency documented: the DBA program chart lists 'BA 388' among the 18 core courses, but the program-content text lists 'BA 391 – Seminar on Higher Education' and states the 54 units comprise '51 credits courses and a 3 credits seminar devoted to Higher Education' (BA 388 is actually 'Graduate Internship in AI Applications in Business Management'); BA 391 is used. Second inconsistency: the program chart places the DBA Qualifying Examination 'upon completion of all required core and 12 units of concentration courses', while the program description text says 'upon completion of all required core and at least 20 credit units of the concentration coursework'; the examination milestone is placed after all core and all 24 concentration units, satisfying both. BA 390 is a core course here; its catalog prerequisites (BA 301, BA 304, BA 307, BA 320, BA 340, and at least two concentration courses) are satisfied by placing it after two concentration courses. BA 501 requires completion of all DBA core and at least four concentration courses. Students whose previous education was not in business may be required to complete additional foundation courses (see MBA program description); these are modeled as external prerequisites.",
